WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Hey, welcome to Planetary and Daily Episode 92 coming to you on June 17th, 2026.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.540
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.340
Older adults taking a daily probiotic with antidepressants showed modestly

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.800
greater reductions in depression and anxiety symptoms than placebo recipients.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:23.460
Researchers are mapping previously uncharacterized chemicals present in everyday foods

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.000
beyond standard nutrient labels. These compounds, termed nutritional dark matter,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.260
could help explain individual differences in disease risk and responses to diet.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.380
Early analyses suggest links to aging pathways and metabolic regulation.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.020
The work draws on expanding databases of food composition generated through advanced

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:51.560
spectrometry. Continued mapping should reveal which of these molecules weren't targeted human studies.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.700
Now, here's something most people get wrong about what is actually in everyday meals.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.860
Most people assume nutrition labels tell us the essential story about what we eat.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.880
In reality, thousands of distinct chemical compounds in food remain completely uncharacterized

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.520
and unlisted. Right now, as you digest your last meal,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.060
your cells are encountering molecules that standard carbohydrate, fat, and protein counts

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:23.900
never capture. Analysis suggests over 26,000 distinct compounds exist across common foods,

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:30.400
but the vast majority still lacking any functional annotation. This hidden complexity helps explain

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.580
why two people can eat similar meals yet show different aging trajectories or disease risks.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.960
Paying closer attention to whole food diversity rather than isolated macronutrients

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.940
offers a practical way to hedge against these unknowns while the research catches up.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.740
New findings on food composition and metabolic health continue to refine how we connect daily

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:57.300
choices with longer-term biology. Swedish researchers engineered the substrate beneath

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:03.460
ultrathrin superconducting films to stabilize the superconducting state. The modified surfaces

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:09.100
maintain superconductivity at higher temperatures and under stronger magnetic fields than unmodified

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:14.940
controls. The approach addresses a long-standing barrier to practical applications in quantum

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:21.700
devices and sensors. Precise sculpting at the nanoscale altered electron fawn on interactions

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:27.340
in the material. Next steps include scaling the technique to larger device architectures.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:34.000
A new pretreatment allows cleaner removal of single atomic layers from molybdenum disulfide

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.740
during plasma processing. The coding protects underlying layers while enabling selective etching

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:45.840
required for advanced chip fabrication. The method reduces defects that previously limited yield

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.860
in ultrathrin semiconductor production. Researchers demonstrated improved control over final

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:58.080
device thickness and electronic properties. Integration into existing foundry workflows is now

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:04.820
under evaluation. Insulin resistance and elevated glucose impair brain energy metabolism while

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:10.680
promoting vascular damage and inflammation. Certain diabetes medications have shown signals

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:16.780
of reduced dementia incidents in observational data. The connections run in both directions with

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.880
neurodegenerative changes potentially worsening glucose control. Researchers highlight shared mechanisms

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.400
involving mitochondrial function and blood brain barrier integrity. On-going studies aim to test

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:35.300
whether tighter metabolic management measurably alters cognitive trajectories. On a different note,

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:41.680
detailed lipid profiling of several millet varieties uncovered previously undetected lipid classes.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.920
Some of these compounds demonstrated anti-inflammatory and glucose lowering activity in preliminary

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:54.000
assays. The findings add to evidence that millet's deliver benefits beyond their known fiber

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.540
and mineral content. Climate-resilient millet cultivation may therefore carry additional

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:07.120
nutritional advantages for populations at metabolic risk. Follow-up work will examine bioavailability

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:13.980
and effects in human feeding studies. Analysis of circulating NAD plus levels across age groups

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:21.340
found weak correlations with established measures of biological age. The data suggests tissue-specific

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:28.920
NAD plus dynamics are not reliably captured in standard blood draws. Researchers compared NAD plus

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:36.020
readings against multiple epigenetic and proteomic clocks. The results indicate that direct supplementation

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:43.340
trials may need more precise endpoints than circulating NAD plus. Future biomarker panels will likely

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:50.320
incorporate additional intermediates or tissue-specific readouts. A small clinical trial tested probiotic

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:57.020
supplementation alongside standard antidepressant treatment in seniors. Participants receiving the probiotic

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.180
experience slightly larger improvements in both depression and anxiety scores compared with those

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:08.120
given placebo. The study focused on adults already managing depressive symptoms through conventional

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:14.760
medication. Researchers noted the effect size remained modest yet consistent across measured outcomes.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:21.000
Further trials will need to clarify optimal strains, dosing, and duration before broader

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.160
recommendations emerge. An upcoming research cruise will collect new observations of circulation

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:33.480
strength between the Mediterranean and North Atlantic. Models project substantial weakening

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:39.920
of the AMOC under continued warming with consequences for European and global climate patterns.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:46.960
The expedition targets early detection of shifts in deep water formation. Data will help constrain

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:53.200
uncertainty in current climate projections. Results are expected to inform updated risk assessments

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:59.560
for regional weather extremes. Advanced simulations reproduce mature heat waves yet missed the

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:06.480
proceeding dynamical setup that initiates them. The gap produces forecast skill several days ahead of

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.850
temperatures. Researchers identified specific moisture and circulation patterns that

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:18.370
current models under resolve. Improved representation of these processes could extend reliable warnings

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:25.330
for vulnerable populations. Targeted model development is already underway using recent extreme events

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:31.650
as test cases. Researchers produce ground level light estimates that account for individual tree

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:39.030
crowns and terrain features. The maps differentiate light availability inside forests from open areas with

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:44.950
fine spatial detail. Applications range from ecological modeling to solar energy sighting and

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:50.570
microclimate studies. Validation against field measurements confirmed accuracy across varied

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:56.890
vegetation types. The data set is now available for integration into broader environmental analyses.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:02.770
An international team examined why some introduce plant species established successfully

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:07.790
while close relatives fail. Incorporating data on dark diversity,

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:14.150
species present in the regional pool but absent locally, improved predictions of invasion outcomes.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:19.730
The approach reconciles earlier contradictory findings on phylogenic relatedness

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:26.030
and establishment success. Field data from multiple continents supported the revised framework.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:32.530
Further tests will apply the method to animal taxa and changing climates. Rice university

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:37.390
scientists developed a barcording technique that links phages to their bacterial hosts

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:43.710
without culturing either. The method revealed previously unknown infection networks within complex

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:49.970
communities. These connections open routes for precision microbiome editing using targeted phages.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:56.150
The approach scales to natural samples containing hundreds of species. Validation experiments

00:07:56.150 --> 00:08:02.370
confirm specificity across diverse bacterial phyla. Researchers trained a model that generates

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:09.210
candidate structures from raw spectra and scores their chemical plausibility. The open tool reduces the

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:15.750
time required for manual interpretation from hours to minutes. Performance was demonstrated on multiple

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:22.210
classes of organic and inorganic compounds. Integration with existing laboratory workflows is

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:28.350
straightforward via web interface. Continued training on larger spectral libraries should further

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:34.250
improve accuracy. New classification accounts for temperature anomalies at depth rather than

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:40.270
surface measurements alone. Subsurface heat waves can persist after surface conditions normalize,

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:47.850
altering oxygen and nutrient profiles. The framework helps managers anticipate impacts on fisheries

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:53.610
and benthic communities. Data from the Virginia coast illustrated distinct vertical signatures

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:59.570
across events. Expanded monitoring arrays will test the scheme in additional regions.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:05.390
The intervention targets inflammation driving blood vessels in the knee through embolization.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:11.310
Patients reported significant pain reduction and better function that persisted 12 months post

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:17.590
procedure. No serious adverse events occurred in the studied cohort. The approach offers an option

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:23.630
for those not yet ready for joint replacement. Investigators plan larger randomized trials to

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:30.810
confirm durability and identify ideal candidates. Before we go, keep an eye on upcoming work examining

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:37.030
superconducting films and Atlantic circulation patterns. That's Planetarian Daily for Today.

